flowchart TB
    accTitle: The Releases page
    accDescr: Every day, and with every change of main, the Docs workflow builds this website. Its hooks ask the API of GitHub once for the releases of every project with their notes, leave out drafts and prereleases, and keep of the notes only text, lists, headings, tables, code and links to https. They write the latest five releases of every project into the Releases page, and the latest release of every project with the headline of its notes into What's new on the home pages. Without the API, the page links the releases of every project on GitHub, and the build passes. As a page loads in a reader's browser, docs/javascripts/projects.js reads repos.json of the dashboard, adds a release that came out after the build with a link to its notes on GitHub, and tells the day of every release as the time since.

    build(["The Docs workflow<br>every day and with<br>every change of main"])
    api["api.github.com<br>the releases of every<br>project with their notes"]
    hooks["The hooks of the website<br>no draft, no prerelease,<br>only text, lists, code<br>and links to https"]
    page["The Releases page<br>the latest five releases<br>of every project"]
    news["What's new<br>the latest release of every<br>project with its headline"]
    offline["No API<br>a link to the releases<br>of every project on GitHub"]
    data["/repo-blueprint/dashboard/<br>repos.json"]
    script["projects.js<br>in the reader's browser"]
    newer["A newer release<br>with a link to its notes,<br>every day as the time since"]

    build --> hooks
    api --> hooks
    hooks --> page & news
    hooks -. "no answer" .-> offline
    page & news --> script
    data --> script
    script --> newer

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class build,hooks,script bot
    class offline person
    class page,news,newer done
